-- Equilibration of a seven-component gas condensate from COMPVD over a water
-- zone. Every COMPVD row names the vapour, so the phase flag - not the datum's
-- side of the gas-oil contact - selects the equation-of-state root; the datum
-- at 2500 m lies below the water-oil contact at 2450 m, so it states the water
-- pressure and the hydrocarbon takes its pressure at the contact. Above the
-- contact the column keeps the connate water of the saturation function, below
-- it the pore space holds water alone. There are no wells; the few short time
-- steps only verify that the initial state is stable.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
