------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Every block vector the compositional simulator fills, at the top of the
-- column (1), the two cells straddling the water-oil contact (30 and 31) and
-- the bottom of the water (40), plus the field average pressure. The gas-oil
-- and water-oil contacts coincide here, so cell 30 holds the vapour COMPVD
-- names with its connate water and cell 31 holds water alone; the pressure and
-- density vectors there pin the change of hydrostatic gradient across the
-- contact. There is no oil zone, so the oil vectors are zero throughout and
-- pin the phase-absent path. Nothing moves over this schedule; the vectors
-- pin the equilibrated state.

FPR

BPR
 1 1 1 /
 1 1 30 /   -- above the water-oil contact
 1 1 31 /   -- below it
 1 1 40 /
/

